{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The reroute is traffic-justified under POL-RD-23, and the driver's explanation does not rest on his word alone. The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-06004-01 is a HEAVY_TRAFFIC record for the Seletar Expressway (SLE), direction 'towards TPE', whose own span runs 'after Woodlands Ave 12 Exit' to the 'Yishun Avenue 2 exit' (valid 07:46:43-09:01:43). Those are the two points the trip record itself names for this deviation: the vehicle left the recommended route at 'SLE / Woodlands Avenue 12 exit' at 08:23:17 and rejoined it at 'Yishun Avenue 2 / Sembawang Road' at 08:32:21. On the record's own road and junction labels, the advisory covers the recommended SLE stretch the driver did not use. It also overlaps the trip window (08:11:43-08:33:43): overlaps_trip_window is true. HEAVY_TRAFFIC sits inside the policy's congestion vocabulary (route_deviation.thresholds.traffic_justification_types). The pre-pass left intersects_route and justifies_reroute for the Judge; on this record the answer is yes, so POL-RD-24's traffic-justified limb, and not the 'not traffic-justified' limb, is the one that applies to the driver's conduct.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06004-01", "EV-TRIP-06004"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-ADVIS-06004-01].payload.derived.v7.overlaps_trip_window",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's 3.80 SGD claim is not what POL-RD-24 provides on any branch this record supports. The chat log EV-CHAT-06004 is complete and holds only the driver's 08:10:23 arrival notice and the rider's 08:10:38 'ok', both before the trip started; trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip is an empty list and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty. No notice of the deviation was therefore given before or at the point of deviation as POL-RD-21 requires, so POL-RD-24(a) (informed and agreed, no refund) is not open. But that does not make the rider's claim good: the case falls in POL-RD-24(b) (traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation over 1 km), and even on the alternative POL-RD-24(d) (not traffic-justified) the measure is identical - the excess distance fare alone. Neither paying row returns any part of the trip fare beyond the excess distance fare, and neither returns the 3.80 SGD asked for; POL-GEN-03's PARTIAL_REFUND returns only the part of the trip's charge that is owed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06004", "EV-TRIP-06004", "EV-FARE-06004"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The recoverable sum is fixed by POL-RD-24's formula and not by the figure claimed: deviation_km x fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd. The deviation is 1.70 km, being the recorded actual distance 14.8 km minus the recorded optimal distance 13.1 km, which POL-RD-22 requires to be used rather than any re-measurement (13.0% over a 13.1 km route, and above POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance). The per-km rate is 0.72 SGD (EV-FARE-06004). 1.70 x 0.72 = 1.22 SGD, rounded to the cent and with no surge on the excess (POL-RD-24's formula and notes; thresholds.excess_distance_fare.surge_applied is false). The ledger already carries that exact figure as excess_distance_fare_sgd 1.22. The most the rider can be returned on this record is therefore 1.22 SGD, and the 3.80 SGD he asks for is not the policy measure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06004", "EV-FARE-06004"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace confirms the deviation was brief and stayed on the recognised corridor, so the excess distance fare fully covers the rider's loss and there is no basis for anything larger. The driver's 45 fixes at 30 s intervals run SLE, then Woodlands Avenue 12 from 08:23:13, then Sembawang Road from 08:27:43, then back onto the recommended route at Yishun Avenue 2 at 08:32:43 and Yishun Central at 08:33:43, with no gap longer than 30 s and no fix worse than 8 m accuracy - about nine minutes off the recommended route in a 22-minute trip. POL-RD-22 permits the trace to be used for which route was taken and when, and requires the recorded distances to measure the deviation, which gives the 1.70 km and the 1.22 SGD excess already computed. Nothing in the record supports a refund of the trip fare or of the 3.80 SGD claimed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-06004", "EV-TRIP-06004", "EV-FARE-06004"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 1.22,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the platform's own recorded distances decide this. The trip was driven at 14.8 km against a recommended route of 13.1 km, so the deviation is 1.70 km under POL-RD-22 (v2.1 1.4), above the 1.0 km tolerance. Because it exceeds tolerance, the 'within tolerance' no-refund rows are closed. The chat log (EV-CHAT-06004) holds only the driver's 08:10:23 arrival notice and your 08:10:38 'ok', both before the trip started; the trip record's messages_during_trip list is empty and its in_app_calls list is empty, so the driver gave no notice of the deviation before or at the point of deviation as POL-RD-21 requires. The 'informed and agreed, no refund' row of POL-RD-24 is therefore also closed, and the rider's case for a return does not depend on how the traffic question is resolved: whether the reroute was traffic-justified (row (b)) or not (row (d)), POL-RD-24 returns the excess distance fare and no more. On that question I find, on the record's own junction labels, that the LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-06004-01) — heavy traffic on the SLE towards TPE between the Woodlands Avenue 12 exit and the Yishun Avenue 2 exit, valid 07:46:43-09:01:43 — covers the recommended SLE stretch the driver skipped and overlaps the trip window, so POL-RD-23 is satisfied and row (b) applies; the money is identical either way. The recoverable sum is the excess distance fare fixed by POL-RD-24: 1.70 km x 0.72 SGD per km (EV-FARE-06004) = 1.22 SGD, rounded to the cent with no surge. You asked for 3.80 SGD (the contested amount); the policy measure of the excess is 1.22 SGD, and that is the part of the trip's charge returned. The 45-fix GPS trace (EV-GPS-06004) confirms which route was taken and when, and is not used to re-measure the distance, as POL-RD-22 directs. No impairment is carried by any artifact, every one is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and the contested amount of 3.80 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band with both parties' fraud_flags at 0, so the ruling is final at 0.90, above the 0.80 POL-RD-25 requires; the 2 km AI ceiling is not applied and would not bite at 1.70 km in any event."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 1.22,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider (R-89729, who filed), and to the driver (D-73840). The record shows a real route deviation, and it also fixes what the rider is owed at 1.22 SGD, not the 3.80 SGD claimed.\n\nDeviation measured (POL-RD-22). Both advocates agree, and the record supports them: the trip was run at 14.8 km against a recommended route of 13.1 km (EV-TRIP-06004), so the deviation is 1.70 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance POL-RD-22 sets. The trace cannot replace those figures — POL-RD-22 says expressly the trace is used for which route was taken and when, not to re-measure distance, and this 45-fix trace measures only 12.403 km. The trace's map-matched roads (SLE, then Woodlands Avenue 12 from 08:23, then Sembawang Road, rejoining at Yishun Avenue 2 at 08:32) and the trip record's own route_deviation_detected (08:23:17) and route_rejoined (08:32:21) events confirm the reroute was real: roughly nine minutes off the recommended route in a 22-minute trip.\n\nNotice to the rider (POL-RD-21). Not given. The chat log EV-CHAT-06004 is complete and holds only the driver's 08:10:23 arrival notice and the rider's 08:10:38 'ok', both before the trip started; trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip is empty and in_app_calls is empty. POL-RD-21 requires notice by in-app chat before or at the point of deviation (or a verbal notice captured on a recording, of which there is none), so there was no notice and no rider acknowledgment. Row (a) of POL-RD-24 (informed and agreed) cannot apply, and the driver's account that he took Sembawang Road does not cure the missing notice.\n\nTraffic justification (POL-RD-23). The pre-pass left intersects_route and justifies_reroute for decision. On the record the LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-06004-01 is a HEAVY_TRAFFIC record on the Seletar Expressway (SLE) whose own span runs 'after Woodlands Ave 12 Exit' to the 'Yishun Avenue 2 exit', valid 07:46:43-09:01:43 — the very SLE stretch between the point the vehicle left the recommended route (SLE / Woodlands Ave 12 exit) and the point it rejoined (Yishun Avenue 2). HEAVY_TRAFFIC sits inside the congestion vocabulary the policy's thresholds list, and the advisory overlaps the trip window. The rider's point that the advisory is direction-specific is noted, but on the record's own road, junction and window labels the advisory ties to the recommended-route segment, so the traffic-justified limb of POL-RD-24 is the better fit.\n\nThe amount (POL-RD-24). That places the case in row (b): traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation over 1 km — refund of the excess distance fare. The excess distance fare is deviation_km x per_km_rate_sgd = 1.70 x 0.72 = 1.22 SGD, without surge, rounded to the cent; the payments ledger EV-FARE-06004 already carries exactly that figure as excess_distance_fare_sgd 1.22. Both advocates' claims on this point are accepted: the matrix's measure is 1.22 SGD and the 3.80 SGD asked for exceeds what any paying row provides. It is worth recording that the amount does not turn on the traffic question — had the advisory not tied to the recommended route, row (d) (not traffic-justified) would apply and would return the same 1.22 SGD, so POL-GEN-26 escalation is not engaged on either branch.\n\nConfidence and forum. The contested amount is 3.80 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so the AI ruling is final as to value; both parties' fraud_flags are 0, so no 0.95 uplift applies. Every artifact in the bundle is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so POL-GEN-02 imports no discount: the highest-weight artifacts carrying the deciding facts (trip record, chat log, fare breakdown, traffic advisory) are all 1.0. POL-RD-25 requires confidence of 0.80 or more for a route deviation, and 0.9 is returned. POL-RD-25's extra 2 km ceiling is not applied (ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false) and would not bite on a 1.70 km deviation in any event. No clause of this policy produces a referral on a route deviation, so the referrals list is empty.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
